From f145b29584b342363daa6531ce653e4b7ef4514c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Viktor Semenov <suit.uanic@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 22:56:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 01/45] Add the Specula observer feed hook

With specula.feed set to a Unix socket path, a network client streams a
per-turn view of the simulation to specula-server (feed format v3, see
SpeculaFeed.h). The hook runs after the turn hash is sent and only reads
the simulation, so it cannot change the state hash.

Each turn carries every in-world entity's id, template, position,
angle, owner and minimap colour. Template records name each template
and give its minimap icon. The map size and the terrain (heights, water
level, per-tile texture names) are sent once; CMapReader keeps the
texture names even without a texture manager, which a nonvisual
observer never creates.
